# Numbered ADRs are immutable records (ADR-0024 §Lifecycle rule 1) and are
# written in house style by hand. Their snippets are aligned to be read as
# tables: prettier turns ADR-0013's seven-line factory list into twenty lines of
# wrapped arrow functions, which is correct and unreadable. The index, the
# template and everything else stay formatted.
docs/adr/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md

# Generated
.turbo/
dist/
dist-types/
.next/

# A session parks a git worktree of this same repository here: a whole second
# checkout, untracked, on a branch that is usually mid-step. Formatting it is
# formatting somebody else's working tree — `format:check` fails in every
# session over files git does not track, and `format` would write into a branch
# nobody in this tree is on. `.git/info/exclude` and `scripts/docs-hygiene.mjs`
# skip the same path.
.claude/worktrees/

# shadcn/ui primitives are generated code that this repository owns rather than
# depends on (ADR-0031). Upgrading one is "regenerate and diff", so the local
# copy stays byte-identical to what the CLI emits — reformatting it would put
# prettier's opinions in the way of every future upstream diff. Deliberate
# divergences carry a comment saying so.
packages/ui/src/components/
packages/ui/src/hooks/

# TanStack Router's generated route tree (ADR-0032), one per SPA. It is
# regenerated by `dev` and `build` and never hand-edited, so formatting it means
# `pnpm format` and the generator take turns dirtying the working tree. Lint
# excludes it for the same reason.
#
# A line per app rather than a glob: the entry is the same shape each time, and
# an `apps/*/src/app/routeTree.gen.ts` pattern would silently exempt a
# hand-written file that happened to take the name.
apps/admin/src/app/routeTree.gen.ts
apps/customer/src/app/routeTree.gen.ts

# The desktop app's session outputs (`Claude outputs/`): notes a session
# writes for the operator beside the repository, never part of it. Ignored
# here, in .prettierignore (format:check walks untracked files too) and in
# .dockerignore.
Claude outputs/
